        "marker_at": "w:They"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b2",
      "function": "problem",
      "scene_type": "gs_phases",
      "spoken": "People often even claim it is the only structure you can see from space. NASA calls that a myth as well. Let's start far away. From the Moon, NASA says, the wall is not visible at all. From Earth orbit, it is difficult or impossible to see with the naked eye.",
      "data": {
        "headline": "The further out, the less you see",
        "steps": [
          {
            "label": "From the Moon",
            "sub": "not visible, says NASA",
            "at_word": "Moon"
          },
          {
            "label": "From orbit",
            "sub": "barely, with the naked eye",
            "at_word": "orbit"
          }
        ],
        "rail_dy": 210
      },
      "source_ids": [
        "S1",
        "S2"
      ],
      "overlay": {
        "kicker": "2 · How far out?",
        "marker": "fakt"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b3",
      "function": "explanation",
      "scene_type": "gs_section",
      "spoken": "Distance is only part of the story. The key is contrast, NASA writes. The wall barely stands out from the vegetation and soil around it. Satellite sensors pick it up more easily than the human eye does.",
      "data": {
        "headline": "It is all about contrast",
        "note": "Schematic model",
        "note_dy": 190,
